226→Analysis of the relationship between predicted uncertainty and prediction errors reveals strong negative correlation ($r = -0.563, p < 0.001$), confirming that higher uncertainty appropriately corresponds to larger prediction errors. This inverse relationship validates the utility of uncertainty estimates for identifying unreliable predictions in operational scenarios, enabling quality-controlled snow cover mapping where low-confidence predictions can be flagged for additional validation.
