/scratch/gdemil24/CVPR_sentinel_Fusion/ISPR_Paper_latex/sec/4_Result.tex:49:We compare our hybrid CNN-Transformer architecture against three baseline architectures to validate the effectiveness of our design combining cross-modal attention fusion, multi-resolution processing, and quality-aware learning. \added{To ensure fair comparison, all models, including baselines, are trained and evaluated under identical conditions: inputs are aggregated from native 10m resolution to 60m using mean pooling over $6 \times 6$ pixel blocks, and all models predict against the same 60m GFSC reference labels. The multi-resolution guided disaggregation described in Section~\ref{sec:multi_resolution} is an inference-time post-processing capability applied \textit{after} the core prediction; it is not used during training or quantitative evaluation. Thus, any performance differences in Table~\ref{tab:sota_comparison} and Table~\ref{tab:ablation} reflect purely architectural contributions (cross-attention fusion, transformer layers, quality-aware learning), not resolution-handling advantages.} Table~\ref{tab:sota_comparison} presents test set results across 18,117 patches from 4 geographically separated tiles.
