/scratch/gdemil24/CVPR_sentinel_Fusion/ISPR_Paper_latex/sec/4_Result.tex:272:\added{Table~\ref{tab:cloud_robustness} presents results on all 18,117 test patches. XFuse under complete S2 occlusion achieves \textbf{83.2\%} accuracy, only 8.7 percentage points below full S1+S2 performance and \textbf{higher than Early Fusion operating with its complete multi-modal input (81.3\%)}. This result demonstrates that the bidirectional cross-attention mechanism internalises complementary SAR-optical representations: when optical data is unavailable, attention weights shift to prioritise S1 features, maintaining meaningful snow discrimination. Concatenation-based baselines (Early Fusion, CNN-Only) have no analogous adaptive mechanism: they treat both modalities symmetrically and cannot compensate for a missing modality.}
